## Scheduling agents

`preview_schedule` turns phrases such as `daily at 09:00`, `weekdays at 9am`,
`every 2 hours at minute 15` or `once at 2026-08-01 14:00` into occurrences;
use it before `create_agent` or a schedule change. `create_agent` takes a name,
provider (`claude` or `codex`), schedule and optional workspace, prompts,
model, permission mode, overlap (`replace` or `parallel`) and retention timeout.
`run_agent` starts an ordinary run in a new tab; for a loop it requests the next
prompt in the existing instance, creating a tab only for its first run.
`resume_run` reopens a past run's provider session. Dangerous permission modes
can only be set by the person.
`rename_agent` renames one. In OmniTerm's sidebar an agent can sit in a `group`
(`Section` or `Section/Subsection`) and have an `icon` (`sf:<SF Symbol name>`,
